      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion at this exact site",
      "functional_impact_measured": "Confocal microscopy and flow cytometry confirmed robust surface expression of BBS-hERG-YFP in HEK293 cells, with BTX647 surface signals up to 100-fold above threshold; channel processing and surface trafficking were preserved. Explicit electrophysiology of the BBS-tagged construct was not reported in the cited paper.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "L1 (PMC5917007) and L8 (PMC10568093) independently name the identical junction T436/E437 in the S1\u2013S2 extracellular loop (topology 430\u2013453) of full-length membrane-anchored hERG. Python verification confirms aa(436)=T and aa(437)=E in the canonical sequence. The junction sits 7 residues from TM1 end (429) and 17 residues from TM2 start (454), both well above the 3-residue minimum. Disulfide cysteines C445 and C449 lie 9 and 13 residues downstream of the junction and were not disrupted in the published construct. Full-length hERG1a (KCNH2) expressed in HEK293 cells; a 13-residue bungarotoxin-binding site (BBS) was inserted between residues Thr436 and Glu437 in the extracellular S1\u2013S2 loop by site-directed mutagenesis, combined with a C-terminal YFP fusion (BBS-hERG1a-YFP). Surface channels were labeled with Alexa Fluor 647-conjugated bungarotoxin in non-permeabilized cells and quantified by confocal microscopy and flow cytometry. [validation: surface_only; position: validated; source: paper; entailment_verified: True]",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 29725305,
          "citation": "PMID 29725305",
          "claim": "A 13-residue bungarotoxin-binding site (BBS; TGGCGGTACTACGAGAGCAGCCTGGAGCCCTACCCCGAC) ( Sekine-Aizawa and Huganir, 2004 ; Yang et al., 2010 ) was then introduced between residues T436/E437 in the extracellular S1\u2013S2 loop of hERG using the Quik-Change Lightning Site-Directed Mutagenesis Kit (Stratagene) according to the manufacturer\u2019s instructions. 16 LQT2 mutations were introduced in the PAS domain of BBS-hERG-YFP via site-directed mutagenesis."
        }
      ],
