  "literature_notes": "Two extracellular sites in the S1\u2013S2 loop (topology 430\u2013453) are supported by the ledger with exact residue-level evidence. Site 1 (T436/E437, BBS) is grounded by two independent papers (L1/PMC5917007 and L8/PMC10568093) naming the identical junction. Site 2 (T443/E444, HA) is grounded by L7 and corroborated by L9, L11, and L14. The C-terminal YFP fusion described in L2 is intracellular (topology 657\u20131159) and does not qualify as an extracellular tag site. The S3\u2013S4 extracellular span is a single residue (501, topology-derived) and no ledger line reports an insertion there. The S5\u2013S6 turret loop (571\u2013638) is the longest extracellular span but no ledger line reports a tag insertion there for KCNH2 or a close ortholog. Lines L3\u2013L6, L9\u2013L16 were reviewed; they corroborate the two named junctions but do not pin additional distinct positions. The validation_level for Site 2 is elevated to surface_and_function because L11 and L14 explicitly state the HA tag in the S1\u2013S2 loop does not interfere with processing or function, and L7/L9 confirm surface display at this exact junction.",
